égration avec des outils de développement tels que React, Python et Node.js","Compatibilité avec les interfaces de ligne de commande (CLI) pour une plus grande flexibilité"],"de":["Systematische Workflows für die AI-gestützte Entwicklung","Taskorientierter Rahmen mit Qualitäts-Toren","Verbesserung der Qualität und Effizienz in der Entwicklung","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React, Python und Node.js","Kompatibilität mit Kommandozeilen-Schnittstellen (CLI) für eine größere Flexibilität"],"pt":["Fluxos de trabalho sistemáticos para desenvolvimento assistido por ferramentas de IA","Gateways de qualidade para garantir a entrega de código de alta qualidade","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento populares como React, Python e Node.js","Suporte a CLI para automação de tarefas","Análise de código e relatórios de qualidade"],"ru":["Системные рабочие процессы для разработки с помощью ИИ Агентов","Контроли качества для обеспечения поставки высококачественного кода","Интеграция с популярными инструментами разработки seperti React, Python и Node.js","Поддержка CLI для автоматизации задач","Анализ кода и отчеты о качестве"],"ar":["تدفقات عمل منهجية لتطوير مدعوم من أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","بوابات جودة لضمان تسليم كود عالي الجودة","التكامل مع أدوات تطوير شائعة مثل React, Python و Node.js","دعم CLI للتحكم الآلي في المهام","تحليل الكود وتقارير الجودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能工具测试","如何使用AI工具进行测试","AI测试工作流","AI工具与传统测试方法的比较","AI测试安装指南","AI工具测试设置教程"],"ja":["AIエージェントのテスト","AIツールを使用してテストを行う方法","AIテストワークフロー","AIツールと伝統的なテスト方法の比較","AIテストのインストールガイド","AIツールのテスト設定チュートリアル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 테스트","AI 도구를 사용하여 테스트를 수행하는 방법","AI 테스트 워크플로우","AI 도구와 전통적인 테스트 방법의 비교","AI 테스트 설치 가이드","AI 도구 테스트 설정 튜토리얼"],"es":["herramientas de pruebas AI","desarrollo asistido por IA","flujos de trabajo sistemáticos","puertas de calidad","cómo usar herramientas de pruebas AI","alternativas a herramientas de pruebas AI","instalación de herramientas de pruebas AI","guía de configuración de herramientas de pruebas AI"],"fr":["outils de test IA","développement assisté par IA","flux de travail systématiques","portes de qualité","comment utiliser les outils de test IA","alternatives aux outils de test IA","installation des outils de test IA","guide de configuration des outils de test IA"],"de":["AI-Testing-Tools","AI-gestützte Entwicklung","systematische Workflows","Qualitäts-Tore","wie man AI-Testing-Tools verwendet","Alternativen zu AI-Testing-Tools","Installation von AI-Testing-Tools","Einrichtungsanleitung für AI-Testing-Tools"],"pt":["ferramentas de teste","desenvolvimento assistido por IA","fluxos de trabalho sistemáticos","gateways de qualidade","React","Python","Node.js","CLI","análise de código","relatórios de qualidade"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","разработка с помощью ИИ","системные рабочие процессы","контроли качества","React","Python","Node.js","CLI","анализ кода","отчеты о качестве"],"ar":["أدوات الاختبار","تطوير مدعوم من أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تدفقات عمل منهجية","بوابات جودة","React","Python","Node.js","CLI","تحليل الكود","تقارير الجودة"]}},"owner":"shinpr","repo":"agentic-code","repoPath":"shinpr/agentic-code","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T13:13:22.555Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"testing","description":"Applies TDD process, test quality criteria, and mock guidelines. Use when: writing unit tests, using mocks, or reviewing test quality.","bodyPreview":"# Testing Rules\n\n## Language-Specific References\n\nFor language-specific rules, also read:\n- **TypeScript/Vitest**: [references/typescript.md](references/typescript.md)\n\n## TDD Process [MANDATORY for all code changes]\n\n**Execute this process for every code change:**\n\n### RED Phase\n1. Write test that defines expected behavior\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test FAILS (if it passes, the test is wrong)\n\n### GREEN Phase\n1. Write MINIMAL code to make test pass\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test PASSES\n\n### REFACTOR","body":"# Testing Rules\n\n## Language-Specific References\n\nFor language-specific rules, also read:\n- **TypeScript/Vitest**: [references/typescript.md](references/typescript.md)\n\n## TDD Process [MANDATORY for all code changes]\n\n**Execute this process for every code change:**\n\n### RED Phase\n1. Write test that defines expected behavior\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test FAILS (if it passes, the test is wrong)\n\n### GREEN Phase\n1. Write MINIMAL code to make test pass\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test PASSES\n\n### REFACTOR Phase\n1. Improve code quality\n2. Run test\n3. Confirm test STILL PASSES\n\n### VERIFY Phase [MANDATORY - 0 ERRORS REQUIRED]\n1. Execute ALL quality check commands for your language/project\n2. Fix any errors until ALL commands pass with 0 errors\n3. Confirm no regressions\n4. ENFORCEMENT: Cannot proceed with ANY errors or warnings\n\n**Exceptions (no TDD required):**\n- Pure configuration files\n- Documentation only\n- Emergency fixes (but add tests immediately after)\n- Exploratory spikes (discard or rewrite with tests before merging)\n- Build/deployment scripts (unless they contain business logic)\n\n## Basic Testing Policy\n\n### Quality Requirements\n- **Coverage**: Unit test coverage must be 80% or higher\n- **Independence**: Each test can run independently\n- **Reproducibility**: Tests are environment-independent\n\n### Coverage Requirements\n**Mandatory**: Unit test coverage must be 80% or higher\n**Metrics**: Statements, Branches, Functions, Lines\n\n### Test Types and Scope\n1. **Unit Tests**\n   - Verify behavior of individual units (functions, modules, or components)\n   - Mock all external dependencies\n   - Fast execution (milliseconds)\n\n2. **Integration Tests**\n   - Verify coordination between multiple components\n   - Use actual dependencies when appropriate\n   - Test real system interactions\n\n3. **E2E Tests (End-to-End Tests)**\n   - Verify complete user workflows across entire system\n   - Test real-world scenarios with all components integrated\n   - Validate system behavior from user perspective\n   - Ensure business requirements are met end-to-end\n\n4. **Cross-functional Verification in E2E Tests** [MANDATORY for feature modifications]\n\n   **Purpose**: Prevent regression and ensure existing features remain stable when introducing new features or modifications.\n\n   **When Required**:\n   - Adding new features that interact with existing components\n   - Modifying core business logic or workflows\n   - Changing shared resources or data structures\n   - Updating APIs or integration points\n\n   **Integration Point Analysis**:\n   - **High Impact**: Changes to core process flows, breaking changes, or workflow modifications\n     - Mandatory comprehensive E2E test coverage\n     - Full regression test suite required\n     - Performance benchmarking before/after\n\n   - **Medium Impact**: Data usage modifications, shared state changes, or new dependencies\n     - Integration tests minimum requirement\n     - Targeted E2E tests for affected workflows\n     - Edge case coverage mandatory\n\n   - **Low Impact**: Read-only operations, logging additions, or monitoring hooks\n     - Unit test coverage sufficient\n     - Smoke tests for integration points\n\n   **Success Criteria**:\n   - Zero breaking changes in existing workflows\n   - Performance degradation within project-defined acceptable limits\n   - No new errors in previously stable features\n   - All integration points maintain expected contracts\n   - Backward compatibility preserved where required\n\n## Test Design Principles\n\n### Test Case Structure\n- Tests consist of three stages: **Setup, Execute, Verify** (also known as Arrange-Act-Assert or Given-When-Then)\n- Clear naming that shows purpose of each test\n- One test case verifies only one behavior\n- Test names should describe expected behavior, not implementation\n\n### Test Data Management\n- Manage test data in dedicated directories\n- Define test-specific configuration values\n- Always mock sensitive information (passwords, tokens, API keys)\n- Keep test data minimal, using only data directly related to test case verification\n\n### Test Independence\n- Each test should be able to run in isolation\n- Tests should not depend on execution order\n- Clean up test state after each test\n- Avoid shared mutable state between tests\n\n## Mock and Stub Usage Policy\n\n✅ **Recommended: Mock external dependencies in unit tests**\n- Merit: Ensures test independence and reproducibility\n- Practice: Mock databases, APIs, file systems, and other external dependencies\n- Use framework-appropriate mocking tools\n\n❌ **Avoid: Actual external connections in unit tests**\n- Reason: Slows test speed and causes environment-dependent problems\n- Exception: Integration tests that specifically test external integration\n\n### Mock Decision Criteria\n| Mock Characteristics | Response Policy |\n|---------------------|-----------------|\n| **Simple and stable** | Consolidate in common helpers |\n| **Complex or frequently changing** | Individual implementation |\n| **Duplicated in 3+ places** | Consider consolidation |\n| **Test-specific logic** | Individual implementation |\n\n## Test Granularity Principles\n\n### Core Principle: Observable Behavior Only\n**MUST Test**:\n- Public APIs and contracts\n- Return values and outputs\n- Exceptions and error conditions\n- External calls and side effects\n- Persisted state changes\n\n**MUST NOT Test**:\n- Internal implementation details not exposed publicly\n- Internal state that''s not observable from outside\n- Algorithm implementation details\n- Framework/library internals\n\n### Test Failure Response Decision Criteria\n\n**Fix tests when:**\n- Expected values are wrong\n- Tests reference non-existent features\n- Tests depend on implementation details\n- Tests were written only for coverage\n\n**Fix implementation when:**\n- Tests represent valid specifications\n- Business logic requirements have changed\n- Important edge cases are failing\n\n**When in doubt**: Confirm with stakeholders or domain experts\n\n## Test Implementation Best Practices\n\n### Naming Conventions\n- Test files: Follow your language/framework conventions\n- Test suites: Names describing target features or situations\n- Test cases: Names describing expected behavior (not implementation)\n\n### Test Code Quality Rules\n\n✅ **Recommended: Keep all tests always active**\n- Merit: Guarantees test suite completeness\n- Practice: Fix problematic tests and activate them\n\n❌ **Avoid: Skipping or commenting out tests**\n- Reason: Creates test gaps and incomplete quality checks\n- Solution: Either fix the test or completely delete if truly unnecessary\n\n## Test Quality Criteria [MANDATORY]\n\n1. **Boundary coverage**: Include empty/zero/max/error cases with happy paths\n2. **Literal expectations**: Use literal values in assertions, not computed expressions\n   - Expected value ≠ mock return value (implementation processes data)\n3. **Result verification**: Assert return values and state, not call order\n4. **Meaningful assertions**: Every test must have at least one assertion\n5. **Mock external I/O only**: Mock DB/API/filesystem, use real internal utilities\n\n### Test Helper Guidelines\n\n**Basic Principles**\nTest helpers should reduce duplication and improve maintainability.\n\n**Usage Examples**\n- Builder patterns for test data creation\n- Custom assertions for domain-specific validation\n- Shared setup/teardown utilities\n- Common mock configurations\n\n## Quality Check Commands [MANDATORY for VERIFY phase]\n\n**Execute quality checks appropriate for your language and project setup:**\n\n### Required Quality Checks\nYour project MUST have mechanisms to verify:\n\n1. **All Tests Pass**\n   - Unit tests execute successfully\n   - Integration tests (if applicable) pass\n   - No test failures or errors\n\n2. **Code Builds Successfully**\n   - Compilation succeeds (for compiled languages)\n   - No build errors or warnings\n\n3. **Code Style Compliance**\n   - Linting rules are satisfied\n   - Formatting standards are met\n   - Style guide adherence verified\n\n4. **Type Safety** (for typed languages)\n   - Type checking passes\n   - No type errors or warnings\n\n### ENFORCEMENT\n- Cannot proceed with task completion if ANY quality check fails\n- Must fix all errors and warnings before marking task complete\n- If your project lacks certain quality tools, establish them or document the gap\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T13:48:53.295Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT that require rigorous testing protocols for reliable code development.","zh":"非常适合需要严格测试协议以实现可靠代码开发的AI Agent，如Claude Code和AutoGPT。","ja":"Claude CodeやAutoGPTなど、信頼性の高いコード開発に厳格なテストプロトコルを必要とするAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Claude Code 및 AutoGPT와 같이 신뢰할 수 있는 코드 개발을 위해 엄격한 테스트 프로토콜이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren protocolos de prueba rigurosos para el desarrollo de código confiable.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT qui nécessitent des protocoles de test rigoureux pour un développement de code fiable.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die strenge Testprotokolle für zuverlässige Code-Entwicklung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e AutoGPT que exigem protocolos de teste rigorosos para o desenvolvimento de código confiável.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, которые требуют строгих протоколов тестирования для надежной разработки кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يحتاجون إلى بروتوكولات اختبار صارمة لتطوير كود موثوق"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement Test-Driven Development (TDD) using systematic workflows, quality gates, and language-specific references like TypeScript/Vitest, allowing for efficient validation of expected behavior through RED, GREEN, and REFACTOR phases.","zh":"使Agent能够使用系统化的工作流、质量门禁和特定语言的参考（如TypeScript/Vitest）来实施测试驱动开发（TDD），从而通过RED、GREEN和REFACTOR阶段高效验证预期行为。","ja":"体系的なワークフロー、品質ゲート、TypeScript/Vitestなどの言語固有のリファレンスを使用してテスト駆動開発（TDD）を実装する能力をエージェントに付与し、RED、GREEN、REFACTORのフェーズを通じて期待される動作を効率的に検証できるようにします。","ko":"체계적인 워크플로우, 품질 게이트 및 TypeScript/Vitest와 같은 언어별 참조를 사용하여 테스트 주도 개발(TDD)을 구현할 수 있도록 에이전트를 지원하며, RED, GREEN 및 REFACTOR 단계를 통해 예상 동작을 효율적으로 검증할 수 있게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes implementar el Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD) utilizando flujos de trabajo sistemáticos, puertas de calidad y referencias específicas de lenguaje como TypeScript/Vitest, lo que permite una validación eficiente del comportamiento esperado a través de las fases RED, GREEN y REFACTOR.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre le Développement Dirigé par les Tests (TDD) en utilisant des flux de travail systématiques, des portes de qualité et des références spécifiques à la langue comme TypeScript/Vitest, ce qui permet une validation efficace du comportement attendu à travers les phases RED, GREEN et REFACTOR.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, Test-Driven Development (TDD) mithilfe systematischer Workflows, Qualitätsprüfungen und sprachspezifischer Referenzen wie TypeScript/Vitest umzusetzen, was eine effiziente Überprüfung des erwarteten Verhaltens durch die Phasen RED, GREEN und REFACTOR ermöglicht.","pt":"Permite que os agentes implementem o Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD) usando fluxos de trabalho sistemáticos, portões de qualidade e referências específicas de linguagem, como TypeScript/Vitest, permitindo a validação eficiente do comportamento esperado por meio das fases RED, GREEN e REFACTOR.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовать Разработку, управляемую тестированием (TDD), используя системные рабочие процессы, ворота качества и языково-специфические ссылки, такие как TypeScript/Vitest, что позволяет эффективно проверять ожидаемое поведение через фазы RED, GREEN и REFACTOR.","ar":"تمكّن العميل من تنفيذ التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD) باستخدام تدفقات العمل المنهجية وبوابات الجودة والمراجع المحددة للغة مثل TypeScript/Vitest، مما يسمح بالتحقق الفعال من السلوك المتوقع من خلال مراحل RED و GREEN و REFACTOR."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating unit testing with Vitest","Implementing TDD for every code change","Validating test coverage for minimal code changes"],"zh":["使用Vitest自动化单元测试","为每次代码变更实施TDD","验证最小代码变更的测试覆盖率"],"ja":["Vitestを使用した単体テストの自動化","すべてのコード変更に対するTDDの実装","最小限のコード変更に対するテストカバレッジの検証"],"ko":["Vitest를 사용한 단위 테스트 자동화","모든 코드 변경에 TDD 구현","최소 코드 변경에 대한 테스트 커버리지 검증"],"es":["Automatización de pruebas unitarias con Vitest","Implementación de TDD para cada cambio de código","Validación de la cobertura de pruebas para cambios mínimos de código"],"fr":["Automatisation des tests unitaires avec Vitest","Mise en œuvre de TDD pour chaque modification de code","Validation de la couverture des tests pour des modifications minimales de code"],"de":["Automatisierung von Einheitstests mit Vitest","Implementierung von TDD für jeden Code-Change","Validierung der Testabdeckung für minimale Code-Änderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar testes unitários com Vitest","Implementar TDD para cada alteração de código","Validar cobertura de teste para alterações mínimas de código"],"ru":["Автоматизировать модульное тестирование с помощью Vitest","Реализовать TDD для каждого изменения кода","Проверять покрытие тестирования для минимальных изменений кода"],"ar":["تحسين الاختبارات الوحدوية مع Vitest","تنفيذ TDD لكل تغيير في الكود","التحقق من تغطية الاختبار لأقل التغييرات في الكود"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to TDD process","Language-specific rules must be followed (e.g., TypeScript/Vitest)"],"zh":["需要遵循TDD流程","必须遵循特定语言的规则（例如TypeScript/Vitest）"],"ja":["TDDプロセスへの準拠が必要","言語固有のルールに従う必要がある（例：TypeScript/Vitest）"],"ko":["TDD 프로세스를 준수해야 함","언어별 규칙을 따라야 함(예: TypeScript/Vitest)"],"es":["Requiere adherencia al proceso TDD","Las reglas específicas del lenguaje deben seguirse (por ejemplo, TypeScript/Vitest)"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au processus TDD","Les règles spécifiques à la langue doivent être suivies (par exemple, TypeScript/Vitest)"],"de":["Erfordert Einhaltung des TDD-Prozesses","Sprachspezifische Regeln müssen befolgt werden (z. B. TypeScript/Vitest)"],"pt":["Exige aderência ao processo TDD","Regras específicas de linguagem devem ser seguidas (por exemplo, TypeScript/Vitest)"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения процесса TDD","Языково-специфические правила должны быть соблюдены (например, TypeScript/Vitest)"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بعملية TDD","يجب اتباع قواعد اللغة المحددة (على سبيل المثال TypeScript/Vitest)"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"c00c61d5495028896a1e191dafb79997401177466392a655a2f03587407ad460","qualityScore":35}');
